id: DRAFT-E654-ohos-chardev-pollout-select-hang
category: platform, compat, runtime
build_system: makefile|custom
phase: runtime
match_keywords: /dev/null hang, stdout redirect hang, poll POLLOUT, select never returns, EVENTPOLL, char device writability, /dev/zero hang, radamsa hang, fuzzer hangs with stdout redirected, poll then write, owl lisp, do_poll, write readiness
error_signature: "process hangs (State=S, wchan=EVENTPOLL, CPU time frozen) exactly when stdout is redirected to /dev/null or /dev/zero; same command with stdout to a pipe or regular file completes normally"
error_excerpt: "echo 'x' | radamsa --seed 42 -n 1000 -o - > /dev/null never returns; /proc/<pid>/wchan=EVENTPOLL; the VM's poll(2)/select(2) call on the stdout fd never reports writability because OHOS never signals POLLOUT for character devices"
root_cause: "OHOS musl/kernel never reports POLLOUT (writability) for character devices: poll(fd=/dev/null or /dev/zero, POLLOUT) returns 0 revents at any finite timeout and select()/poll() with infinite timeout never return at all — while write(2) to the same fd succeeds and POLLIN on /dev/null as well as POLLOUT on pipes and regular files all behave correctly. Runtimes that implement non-blocking ports as poll-then-write (Owl Lisp VM do_poll using select(nfds,...,NULL); same pattern possible in other script-language VMs and event loops) therefore sleep forever as soon as stdout is redirected to /dev/null or /dev/zero."
rec_approach: "Inside the runtime's poll/select wrapper, pre-check each fd in the WRITE set with fstat(): if S_ISCHR(st.st_mode), treat the fd as immediately writable and return without calling select/poll. Keep pipes, sockets and regular files on the native path (their POLLOUT reporting is correct on OHOS, and pipes need real backpressure). This is a ~14-line patch at the single choke point where the VM maps Scheme ports to poll(fd)."
solution: "See archives/r/radamsa/0.7/patches/0001-radamsa-do_poll-ohos-chardev-writable.patch — do_poll() in the generated radamsa.c scans the write set with fstat before select(); S_ISCHR fds return writable immediately. Before the patch tests/1k.sh and any '> /dev/null' usage hung forever; after the patch the full upstream suite passes 28/28 and the '> /dev/null' and '> /dev/zero' regressions are asserted in test_package/test.sh."
fallback: "Avoiding the redirection (> pipe into cat, or > regular file) sidesteps the hang but changes the documented usage contract and still hangs every external user script; the fstat short-circuit is the correct fix."
prescan_pattern: "dev/null.*hang|hangs.*dev/null|select.*never return|POLLOUT"
verify_builds: "radamsa 0.7 on ohos-aarch64 (2026-09-22): clean conan create round, upstream tests/run 28/28 after patch; probe matrix: /dev/null+/dev/zero POLLOUT never ready at timeout 0/100ms/inf, pipes and regular files correct, /dev/null POLLIN correct"
severity: 1
last_updated: 2026-09-22
